meta {
  name: 07 - Cursor Filter Boundary
  type: graphql
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}
  body: graphql
  auth: inherit
}

body:graphql {
  query CursorFilterBoundary {
    justBefore: issues(first: 250, filter: {updatedAt: {gt: "2026-07-30T21:35:03.807Z"}}) { nodes { id updatedAt } }
    exactGt:    issues(first: 250, filter: {updatedAt: {gt: "2026-07-30T21:35:03.808Z"}}) { nodes { id updatedAt } }
    exactGte:   issues(first: 250, filter: {updatedAt: {gte: "2026-07-30T21:35:03.808Z"}}) { nodes { id updatedAt } }
    wideOpen:   issues(first: 250, filter: {updatedAt: {gt: "2020-01-01T00:00:00Z"}}) { nodes { id updatedAt } }
  }
}

docs {
  Reference: https://linear.app/developers/filtering

  Proves the incremental cursor filter is honored, at MILLISECOND precision, and pins down
  the `gt` vs `gte` boundary semantics the connector's checkpoint arithmetic depends on.

  All four issues in this workspace share the byte-identical `updatedAt`
  `2026-07-30T21:35:03.808Z`, which makes this a uniquely sharp boundary test.

  **Limitation / observed finding** (confirmed 2026-07-30):

  | alias        | filter                     | rows |
  |--------------|----------------------------|------|
  | `justBefore` | `gt: ...03.807Z`           | 4    |
  | `exactGt`    | `gt: ...03.808Z`           | 0    |
  | `exactGte`   | `gte: ...03.808Z`          | 4    |
  | `wideOpen`   | `gt: 2020-01-01T00:00:00Z` | 4    |

  So: the filter narrows as documented, sub-second precision IS respected (a 1 ms shift
  flips the result set from 4 rows to 0), `gt` is strictly exclusive, and `gte` is
  inclusive. RFC3339 with a `Z` offset and millisecond precision is accepted verbatim.

  **This table is also the live demonstration of the tied-cursor hazard.** Because all 4
  rows share one `updatedAt`, the two obvious cursor policies both misbehave when a page
  boundary lands inside a tie group:

  - `gt: <last seen updatedAt>` — skips every remaining row sharing that timestamp. If the
    connector had emitted only 2 of these 4 and checkpointed `...03.808Z`, the other 2
    would be lost permanently, exactly as `exactGt` returns 0 rows here.
  - `gte: <last seen updatedAt>` — re-reads the whole tie group on every subsequent sweep,
    forever (`exactGte` returns all 4). Safe against loss, but it cannot make progress if a
    tie group is ever larger than one page.

  Ties are not a corner case on Linear: bulk operations stamp identical `updatedAt` values
  across many rows, which is precisely how this workspace's 4 issues + 3 labels + 6
  workflow states all came to share one millisecond. The connector's cursor policy must
  handle this explicitly — see the plan's "Cursor policy" section.
}

example {
  name: 200 — gt exclusive / gte inclusive at 1ms boundary

  request: {
    url: https://api.linear.app/graphql
    method: POST
    mode: graphql

    body:graphql: {
      query CursorFilterBoundary {
        justBefore: issues(first: 250, filter: {updatedAt: {gt: "2026-07-30T21:35:03.807Z"}}) { nodes { id updatedAt } }
        exactGt:    issues(first: 250, filter: {updatedAt: {gt: "2026-07-30T21:35:03.808Z"}}) { nodes { id updatedAt } }
        exactGte:   issues(first: 250, filter: {updatedAt: {gte: "2026-07-30T21:35:03.808Z"}}) { nodes { id updatedAt } }
        wideOpen:   issues(first: 250, filter: {updatedAt: {gt: "2020-01-01T00:00:00Z"}}) { nodes { id updatedAt } }
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    headers: {
      x-complexity: 9
      x-ratelimit-requests-limit: 2500
      x-ratelimit-requests-remaining: 2493
      x-ratelimit-complexity-limit: 3000000
      x-ratelimit-complexity-remaining: 2999991
    }

    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }

    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": {
            "justBefore": {
              "count": 3,
              "rows": [
                {
                  "id": "adbc7deb-6607-4f39-ade2-c23268dc3ec7",
                  "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T21:35:03.808Z"
                },
                {
                  "id": "86eeb50c-332c-46a7-bebf-a0b67dc346bf",
                  "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T21:35:03.808Z"
                },
                {
                  "id": "4937bc7e-6bda-4612-9a80-3fbaaec872d9",
                  "updatedAt": "2026-08-04T18:12:51.985Z"
                }
              ]
            },
            "exactGt": {
              "count": 1,
              "rows": [
                {
                  "id": "4937bc7e-6bda-4612-9a80-3fbaaec872d9",
                  "updatedAt": "2026-08-04T18:12:51.985Z"
                }
              ]
            },
            "exactGte": {
              "count": 3,
              "rows": [
                {
                  "id": "adbc7deb-6607-4f39-ade2-c23268dc3ec7",
                  "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T21:35:03.808Z"
                },
                {
                  "id": "86eeb50c-332c-46a7-bebf-a0b67dc346bf",
                  "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T21:35:03.808Z"
                },
                {
                  "id": "4937bc7e-6bda-4612-9a80-3fbaaec872d9",
                  "updatedAt": "2026-08-04T18:12:51.985Z"
                }
              ]
            },
            "wideOpen": {
              "count": 3,
              "rows": [
                {
                  "id": "adbc7deb-6607-4f39-ade2-c23268dc3ec7",
                  "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T21:35:03.808Z"
                },
                {
                  "id": "86eeb50c-332c-46a7-bebf-a0b67dc346bf",
                  "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T21:35:03.808Z"
                },
                {
                  "id": "4937bc7e-6bda-4612-9a80-3fbaaec872d9",
                  "updatedAt": "2026-08-04T18:12:51.985Z"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}
